				<title>SCP-5968</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5968</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5968 “Dead Bugs.”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.pinimg.com/originals/b3/99/08/b39908b4bae0623b4c3ea310d5315e49.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;b39908b4bae0623b4c3ea310d5315e49.jpg&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5968 must be placed in a 385mm x W 290mm x H 450mm insect aquarium near Class-D Personnel. Containment room is supervised with security cameras. When Class-D Personnel is deceased, another Class-D is immediately replaced so SCP-5968 does not die from starvation. If SCP-5968 were to die, all Personnel currently suffering from depression must have their rooms searched until SCP-5968 is found.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5968 is an insect that is a dark blue color. SCP-5968 is known for it’s very dark blue color which makes it distinct from other insects. The Specimen seems to have no sentience whatsoever and seems to have the same behavior as regular insects. The specimen is abnormally large compared to it’s counterparts. SCP-5968 takes the form of various insects, usually beetles or roaches. The SCP will also take the form of other insects such as butterflies, mantises and stink bugs. It can also take the form of arachnids too. When SCP-5968 is near any personnel it will be found lurking in said personnel’s area. After long exposure to SCP-5968, Personnel suffer from deep depression and suicidal thoughts. After 1 week of exposure to SCP-5968, Personnel’s skin will turn blue and be unable to speak. 1 day after transitioning, Personnel will be found dead with body hollowed out. Autopsy shows the personnel’s internal organs are missing and all that was left behind is personnel’s skeletal structure and skin. If SCP-5968 is left unsupervised, it will die. DNA sample from SCP-5968’s stomach contents shows that The Sample matches DNA from Personnel. After consumption of Personnel, SCP-5968 will grow slightly by 1 MM. The SCP will continue to grow based on how many personnel it has consumed. It will immediately die after consuming 10. When in death, SCP-5968 leaves behind a dark blue egg found near the body of the personnel. When the egg hatches, the new SCP inside will be any type of insect at random. Reachers must have their memory wiped after contact with SCP-5968&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5968 was discovered Northwest of Mount Fuji, Japan by the [redacted]. Location discovered was in Aokigahara Forest also known as “Suicide Forest.” The year the SCP was discovered was xx/xx/xx. SCP-5968 was found on top of a rock next to a dead body with blue skin. SCP-5968 while manifested as a cockroach was abnormally large and had a dark blue shell. Upon discovery, It seems there are more insects of the same dark blue color in the forest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anonymous51999&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6129980&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1609880796&quot; alt=&quot;Anonymous51999&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6129980)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anonymous51999&quot;  &gt;Anonymous51999&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 05 Jan 2021 12:02:18 +0000</pubDate>
